@{ ViewData["Title"]="Parenting resources"; }
<div class="narrow"><span class="eyebrow">Practical, thoughtful guidance</span><h1>Resources for a clearer record</h1><p class="muted">Small habits that make important details easier to find.</p><article id="record" class="card prose"><span class="tag">GETTING STARTED</span><h2>Building a useful parenting record</h2><p>Write notes close to the event while the details are fresh. Give each entry a specific title and record the date the event occurred.</p><ul><li>Describe what you observed using factual, neutral language.</li><li>Distinguish direct observations from what someone told you.</li><li>Keep original documents and add context for each attachment.</li><li>Use timestamped updates for later information, and a reason when editing.</li></ul><p>Your record is a personal organizational tool. It does not certify the accuracy of an event or provide legal advice.</p></article><article id="privacy" class="card prose"><span class="tag">PRIVACY</span><h2>Sharing with care</h2><p>Share the smallest set of entries needed for a conversation. Check screenshots and documents for unrelated personal information before uploading.</p><p>Invitations require a verified account with the matching email. Bearer links can be opened by anyone who has the link. Set a short expiry, and revoke access when it is no longer needed.</p><p>Recipients may save downloaded material. Revocation prevents future access in the app; it cannot recall copies already saved.</p></article><article id="prepare" class="card prose"><span class="tag">ORGANIZATION</span><h2>Preparing for a conversation</h2><p>Search your timeline and narrow the dates to the relevant period. Review the context and prepare questions before exporting selected entries.</p><p>A PDF is useful for reading; a ZIP also includes the original files and a checksum manifest. Store exports securely and use care when forwarding them.</p></article></div>
